WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.680
( theme music playing )

2
00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.680
( crickets chirping )

3
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.520
Catelyn:
Are you sure about this?

4
00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.560
No.

5
00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.840
It's dangerous.

6
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.480
If we take Tywin's castle from him.

7
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.080
the lords of Westeros
will realize he's not invincible.

8
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.120
Take his home.
take his gold. take his power.

9
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.960
Why are you telling me?

10
00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.560
You begged me not to send Theon

11
00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.160
to negotiate with his father
and I ignored your advice.

12
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.360
Now Winterfell is burnt
to the ground.

13
00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.840
the North is overrun with ironborn.
and Bran and Rickon are gone.

14
00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.680
So Casterly Rock...

15
00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.760
I'm asking your advice.

16
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.320
We have enough men?

17
00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.520
If Walder Frey cooperates.

18
00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:06.400
If Walder Frey cooperates.

19
00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.240
If reinforcements arrive
from King's Landing

20
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.480
before we take the castle...

21
00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.320
we'll be caught between Tywin's army
and the sea.

22
00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.480
We'll lose the war
and die the way Father died.

23
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.480
Or worse.

24
00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.160
Show them how it feels
to lose what they love.

25
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.560
Walder:
My honored guests...

26
00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:15.320
be welcome within my walls
and at my table.

27
00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.920
I extend to you my hospitality

28
00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.680
and protection
in the light of the Seven.

29
00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.080
We thank you for your hospitality.
my lord.

30
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.000
I have come to make my apologies.
my lord.

31
00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.200
and to beg your forgiveness.

32
00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.040
Don't beg my forgiveness. Your Grace.

33
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.920
It wasn't me you spurned.
It was my girls.

34
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.280
One of them was supposed to be queen.
Now none of them are.

35
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.120
This is Arwyen. my daughter.

36
00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.640
My daughter Walda.
my daughter Derwa.

37
00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.240
my daughter Waldra.

38
00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:20.160
My eldest granddaughters
Ginia and Neila.

39
00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.320
Serra and Sarra.
granddaughters. twins.

40
00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:30.000
You could have had either.
Could have had both for all I care.

41
00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.120
My granddaughter Marianne.

42
00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:36.280
My granddaughter Freya.

43
00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.200
My granddaughter... Wertha.

44
00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.160
Waldra.

45
00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.560
- Waldina.
- I'm Merry.

46
00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.320
Fine.

47
00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:55.400
And here's
my youngest daughter Shirei.

48
00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:57.040
though she hasn't bled yet.

49
00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:00.840
Clearly you don't have the patience
for all that.

50
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.480
My ladies. All men should keep
their word. kings most of all.

51
00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:09.960
I was pledged to marry one of you
and I broke that vow.

52
00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.960
The fault is not with you.

53
00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.480
Any man would be lucky
to have any one of you.

54
00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.120
I did what I did not to slight you.
but because I loved another.

55
00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:21.640
I know these words cannot set right

56
00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.720
the wrong I have done to you
and your house.

57
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.280
I beg your forgiveness

58
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:30.120
and pledge to do all I can
to make amends

59
00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.720
so the Freys of the Crossing
and the Starks of Winterfell

60
00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:35.920
may once again be friends.

61
00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.200
Walder:
Very good.

62
00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.600
There she is.

63
00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.640
Come closer.

64
00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.240
Let me have a look at you.

65
00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.480
Still can't see you.

66
00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.240
Old eyes.

67
00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.720
Love.

68
00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:22.320
That's what the Starks of Winterfell
call it. eh?

69
00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.480
( chuckles )

70
00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.200
Very honorable.

71
00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.640
I call it a pretty face.

72
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.360
Mmm. very pretty.

73
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:37.240
Prettier than this lot.
that's for sure.

74
00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.680
Very shapely as well.

75
00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:44.080
Oh. you try to hide her
under that dress.

76
00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.560
If you wanted to hide her.

77
00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:49.960
you shouldn't have brought her here
in the first place.

78
00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.880
I can always see
what's going on beneath a dress.

79
00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.880
Been at this a long time.

80
00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:07.160
I bet when you take that dress off.
everything stays right where it is.

81
00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.600
Doesn't drop an inch.

82
00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:14.400
Your king says
he betrayed me for love.

83
00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:18.080
I say he betrayed me for firm tits
and a tight fit.

84
00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.680
And I can respect that.

85
00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.720
When I was your age.
I'd have broken 50 oaths

86
00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:30.560
to get into that
without a second thought.

87
00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:36.720
Well. I've enough room in the hall
for you lot.

88
00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:38.400
We'll set up tents outside

89
00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.840
with food and ale
for the rest of your men.

90
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.800
Thank you. my lord.

91
00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.400
Well. let's get ready.
The wine will flow red

92
00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:57.200
and the music will play loud
and we'll put this mess behind us.

93
00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.080
- ( horse neighs )
- ( weapons clang )

94
00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.720
- Where?
- There.

95
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.880
There. It's a back gate.

96
00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.160
My men use it when they visit
Yunkai's bed slaves.

97
00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.840
Your men. but not you?

98
00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.480
Daario:
I have no interest in slaves.

99
00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.600
A man cannot make love to property.

100
00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.360
This is where we enter the city.

101
00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.320
Very few guards. They know me.
They let me inside...

102
00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.440
We're not gonna sneak an army
through a back gate.

103
00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.400
I kill the guards.
I take your two best men

104
00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:42.640
and lead them through the back
streets. which I know well.

105
00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.400
and open the front gates.
Then comes the army.

106
00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.520
Once the walls are breached.
the city will fall in hours.

107
00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:52.280
Or perhaps you'll lead Grey Worm
and me to the slaughter.

108
00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.160
cutting the head off our army.

109
00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.760
The masters of Yunkai will pay you
your fee

110
00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.240
and you won't have to split it
three ways

111
00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.040
'cause you've already slaughtered
your partners.

112
00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.720
You have a very suspicious mind.

113
00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:07.880
In my experience.
only dishonest people think this way.

114
00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.280
You command the Unsullied.

115
00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.840
What do you think?

116
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.680
( Daenerys speaking Valyrian )

117
00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:27.520
- You leave tonight.
- Very good.

118
00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:30.680
We'll prepare.

119
00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.400
Ser Jorah.

120
00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.000
You can use an extra sword.

121
00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.480
You're the Queensguard.
Ser Barristan.

122
00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.480
Your place is by the queen.

123
00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:47.760
If we are truly her loyal servants.
we'll do whatever needs to be done

124
00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:51.680
no matter the cost.
no matter our pride.

125
00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.120
We're west of Castle Black.
but the Nightfort's closest to us.

126
00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.360
It was the first castle on the Wall.

127
00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.640
The Watch abandoned it
during the reign of King Jaehaerys I.

128
00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:08.960
Too big. Impossible to maintain.

129
00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.360
Other than Castle Black itself.

130
00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.760
the Nightfort's the perfect castle
for us.

131
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:17.040
It's got a secret sally port.

132
00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.640
the Black Gate.
as old as the Wall itself.

133
00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:23.120
No one's used it in centuries
most likely.

134
00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:27.600
It leads through the Wall
right down into the Nightfort.

135
00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:33.720
if one knows how to find it.
which. it just so happens. I do.

136
00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.320
How do you know all that?

137
00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:43.440
I read about it in a very old book.

138
00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:53.760
You know all that
from staring at marks on paper?

139
00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:55.960
Yes.

140
00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:59.000
You're like a wizard.

141
00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.720
Our father used to tell us

142
00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:19.000
that no wildling ever looked
upon the Wall and lived.

143
00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:22.200
Here we are.

144
00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.360
Alive.

145
00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.760
( donkey braying )

146
00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:42.320
Remember what happens
to children who run.

147
00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.680
I'm your father and I'll do the talking.

148
00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.600
The roads have gone right to hell.
haven't they?

149
00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:58.600
Cracked three spokes this morning.

150
00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:00.560
- Need a hand?
- Need about eight hands.

151
00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.360
Oh!

152
00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.440
Got to get this salt pork
to the Twins

153
00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:07.560
in time for the wedding.

154
00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.400
Many thanks.

155
00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.360
Don't! Don't kill him.

156
00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.560
Dead rats don't squeak.

157
00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:20.200
You're so dangerous. aren't you?
Saying scary things to little girls.

158
00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.800
Killing little boys and old people.

159
00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:24.720
A real hard man you are.

160
00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:28.960
- More than anyone you know.
- You're wrong. I know a killer.

161
00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.320
- A real killer.
- That so?

162
00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:35.400
You'd be like a kitten to him.
He'd kill you with his little finger.

163
00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:38.640
That him?

164
00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.680
- No.
- Good.

165
00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.520
Don't kill him. Please.

166
00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:47.520
Please don't.

167
00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:54.040
You're very kind.
Someday it'll get you killed.

168
00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.320
( groaning )

169
00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.320
( grunts )

170
00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.760
Where are we?

171
00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.840
The Gift. I think.

172
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.040
Brandon the Builder gave
all this land south of the Wall

173
00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:21.040
to the Night's Watch
for their sustenance and support.

174
00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.200
Maester Luwin taught me that.

175
00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.960
Doesn't seem to be supporting
anyone at the moment.

176
00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:30.720
It's good land
and there's no war up here.

177
00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.240
Why leave?

178
00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.400
Wildlings.

179
00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.320
Sorry.

180
00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.960
But they come over the Wall
and raid. steal. carry off women.

181
00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.160
Old Nan said
they turn your skull into a cup

182
00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:46.720
and make you drink your own blood
from it.

183
00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.840
That's what Old Nan said.

184
00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.200
There's a storm coming.

185
00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.840
- I don't see any...
- ( thunder rolling )

186
00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:01.600
It's as good a place to shelter
as any.

187
00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:04.320
We can drink some blood
while we wait.

188
00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:05.960
I don't need much.

189
00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:08.560
( screeching )

190
00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:19.720
Only one old man
and eight good horses.

191
00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:22.360
What's one old man doing
with eight horses?

192
00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.360
He breeds them for the Watch.

193
00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.400
How's he keep folks
from stealing them?

194
00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:29.080
The Watch protects him.

195
00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.880
Not today they don't.

196
00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.600
He's selling horses.
he's got some gold in there.

197
00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.280
- Tormund: And proper steel.
- Let's carve him up.

198
00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:40.360
We just take the horses and go.
The old man's no threat.

199
00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:45.240
- I keep telling you.
- He's an old man.

200
00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:47.360
A spear through the heart's
a better way to die

201
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:51.000
than coughing up your last
with no one but your horses to hear.

202
00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:54.440
The Watch might send a few men
looking for a horse thief.

203
00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.320
They'll send a lot more
to hunt down murderers.

204
00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.120
I hope so.

205
00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:01.880
Killing crows in their castle
is tough.

206
00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:05.360
Killing them out here in the open.
that's what we do.

207
00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:09.440
Spread out.
Surround the hut and move in.

208
00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:35.280
- ( sword clangs )
- ( snorts )

209
00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:37.720
( neighing )

210
00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:51.640
Ygritte!

211
00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.040
Man:
Clear the barn!

212
00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.760
No one's going to believe you're
a hog farmer if you eat them all.

213
00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.560
Best part of the animal.

214
00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:46.760
- Don't worry. They're still there.
- I know they're still there.

215
00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.240
You check every five minutes

216
00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:51.760
like you're afraid
they're gonna move.

217
00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.960
- I'm not afraid.
- Of course you are.

218
00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.480
You're almost there

219
00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.480
and you're afraid
you won't make it.

220
00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:03.440
The closer you get.
the worse the fear gets.

221
00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.120
No point in trying to hide
behind that face.

222
00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:08.920
I know fear when I see it.

223
00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:12.120
Seen it a lot.

224
00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:15.800
I knew fear when I saw it in you.

225
00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:18.720
You're afraid of fire.

226
00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.240
When Beric's sword
went up in flames.

227
00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:24.080
you looked like a scared little girl.

228
00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.640
And I know why. too.

229
00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:33.040
I heard what your brother did to you.

230
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:36.640
Pressed your face to the fire
like you're a nice juicy mutton chop.

231
00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.360
That give you some ideas?

232
00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:47.960
Might do.

233
00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:50.160
Go ahead. then.

234
00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.520
You might get away.

235
00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:55.640
Might even make it there on your own.

236
00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.440
They're just over the river.

237
00:18:58.600 --> 00:18:59.920
The closest you've been to family

238
00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:02.880
since Ilyn Payne snipped
your daddy's neck.

239
00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:09.160
Someday I'm gonna put a sword
through your eye

240
00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:12.360
and out the back of your skull.

241
00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:23.280
( thunder rumbling )

242
00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:25.080
( thunder crashes )

243
00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.800
How are we going to get
past the Wall?

244
00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:40.200
My uncle said it's 700 feet high.

245
00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.120
( thunder crashes )

246
00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.840
How did you get past it?

247
00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.840
Got in a boat
and rowed past the Bay of Seals.

248
00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.000
It would take us two months
to get to the Bay of Seals.

249
00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.920
Some climb straight up the ice.

250
00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:01.200
Even Hodor's not strong enough to
climb the Wall with me on his back.

251
00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:04.480
Hodor.

252
00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.920
- 19 castles guard the Wall.
- ( thunder booms )

253
00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:09.840
- Only three are still manned.
- Hodor!

254
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.920
One of those abandoned fortresses
will give us a way through.

255
00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:14.280
My uncle said the gates were sealed
with ice and stone

256
00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.400
when the castles were deserted.

257
00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:19.040
Well. we'll have
to open them up again.

258
00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:20.600
( hoofbeats. horse neighs )

259
00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:24.240
- Whoa. whoa. whoa!
- Meera: There's a rider out there.

260
00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.240
- Just one?
- ( thunder crashes )

261
00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:27.920
- Meera: There's more.
- Hodor!

262
00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:30.720
( horses neighing )
Shh. Shh.

263
00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:33.400
- It's just thunder. sweet giant.
- Hodor.

264
00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:37.280
- Man: I yield. I yield.
- Wildlings.

265
00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:42.120
( men shouting )

266
00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:43.640
Where's Shaggydog and Summer?

267
00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.680
- Hunting.
- ( horses neighing )

268
00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.640
- ( thunder crashes )
- Hodor!

269
00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.800
- Shh. quiet. Hodor.
- Hodor!

270
00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:51.800
Make him shut up.
If they hear us...

271
00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.960
- Hush. Hodor. No more Hodoring.
- Hodor!

272
00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:56.320
- Hodor!
- Hodor. calm down.

273
00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.200
- You need to keep quiet.
- They're gonna hear us.

274
00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.120
- ( Hodor shouting )
- Bran: Hodor. be quiet.

275
00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.680
( thunder crashes )

276
00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.640
- Ah! Hodor!
- Hodor. calm down.

277
00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:06.400
- Hodor! Hodor!
- Hodor. be quiet!

278
00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.240
What did you do?

279
00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:32.200
Nothing.

280
00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:34.720
I don't know.

281
00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:38.760
( horse screaming )

282
00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:40.720
What's that?

283
00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:42.760
That's a horse dying.

284
00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:55.280
Man:
Bring them over here.

285
00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:58.040
Man #2: That was the last of them.
The rest are dead.

286
00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.280
Orell:
I heard shouting up there.

287
00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:02.320
Thunder.

288
00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.040
I know the difference
between shouting and thunder.

289
00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:08.320
Maybe it's ghosts.
( laughs )

290
00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:14.200
( eagle screeching )

291
00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.440
That won't help you. grandpa.

292
00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:27.480
- Where you riding?
- Doesn't matter now. does it?

293
00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:29.880
No. it doesn't matter now.

294
00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:34.800
Cut his throat
or he'll tell the crows we're here.

295
00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:42.720
You understand.

296
00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:45.200
Let me stand at least.

297
00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:47.320
Let me go with a bit of dignity.

298
00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:53.800
Make the crow kill him.

299
00:22:57.520 --> 00:23:00.440
You're one of us now. Prove it.

300
00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:07.000
The wolves are out there.

301
00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:12.160
I can't do it by choice.

302
00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:15.480
I don't know how.
It happens in my dreams.

303
00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:18.320
You're a warg. Bran.
It's in your blood.

304
00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:23.520
- I can't.
- You just did with him.

305
00:23:23.680 --> 00:23:26.400
A wolf is nothing compared to that.

306
00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:33.720
She looks sharp.

307
00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:38.720
( muttering prayer )

308
00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:45.480
Do it.

309
00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:47.280
Do it.

310
00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:50.320
I told you.
He's still one of them.

311
00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:56.080
Go on. boy.

312
00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:58.440
Go on!

313
00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:03.920
( groans )

314
00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:09.640
He's a crow.
He'll always be a crow.

315
00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:12.400
And here's his crow wife
guarding him.

316
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:16.280
He'll stab us in the back
first chance he gets.

317
00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:20.480
- Kill him.
- ( Jon shouts )

318
00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:35.320
( screaming )

319
00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:37.240
- He's one of them.
- No!

320
00:24:37.400 --> 00:24:39.240
Do you hear me?

321
00:24:39.400 --> 00:24:40.720
( screams )

322
00:24:44.600 --> 00:24:49.320
You're not gonna die
for one of them.

323
00:24:49.480 --> 00:24:51.760
Do it.

324
00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:53.560
They'll find us if you don't.

325
00:24:53.720 --> 00:24:56.240
( swords clanging )

326
00:25:00.760 --> 00:25:03.160
( breathing heavily )

327
00:25:03.320 --> 00:25:05.160
( growling )

328
00:25:13.120 --> 00:25:15.120
( Orell shouts )

329
00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:21.960
( gasps )

330
00:25:22.120 --> 00:25:23.880
You were right the whole time.

331
00:25:24.040 --> 00:25:25.480
( gasps )

332
00:25:25.640 --> 00:25:27.240
( eagle screeches )

333
00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:35.920
( Jon screaming )

334
00:25:48.880 --> 00:25:50.200
Hyah!

335
00:26:09.280 --> 00:26:11.760
Daario: When you hear
a songbird's whistle. you come.

336
00:26:11.920 --> 00:26:15.400
I'm a great whistler.
The greatest in the land.

337
00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:23.200
- ( guard shouts in Valyrian )
- Daario Naharis.

338
00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:38.880
( whistling )

339
00:26:50.440 --> 00:26:52.600
Daario:
That one was quick.

340
00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:56.440
- There may be others.
- I doubt it.

341
00:26:56.600 --> 00:26:59.240
The Yunkish prefer to let their
slaves do their fighting for them.

342
00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:01.040
( guards shouting )

343
00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:45.200
That's what you call a few guards?

344
00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:50.640
( guards shouting )

345
00:27:58.240 --> 00:28:02.800
( men shouting )

346
00:28:08.240 --> 00:28:10.640
Come on!
What do you got. huh?

347
00:28:12.280 --> 00:28:13.680
( cheering )

348
00:29:21.560 --> 00:29:23.600
Lord Edmure...

349
00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:27.560
I hope I'm not a disappointment
to you.

350
00:29:27.720 --> 00:29:30.600
( chuckles )

351
00:29:36.280 --> 00:29:39.600
You're a delight to me. my lady.

352
00:29:39.760 --> 00:29:43.120
You may now cloak the bride
and bring her under your protection.

353
00:30:11.240 --> 00:30:13.360
In the sight of the Seven.

354
00:30:13.520 --> 00:30:19.880
I hereby seal these two souls.
binding them as one for eternity.

355
00:30:20.040 --> 00:30:23.080
Look upon each other
and say the words.

356
00:30:25.480 --> 00:30:27.240
Both:
Father. Smith.

357
00:30:27.400 --> 00:30:29.560
Warrior. Mother.

358
00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:32.920
Maiden. Crone. Stranger...

359
00:30:33.080 --> 00:30:34.760
- I am hers...
- I am his...

360
00:30:34.920 --> 00:30:36.760
- and she is mine...
- and he is mine...

361
00:30:36.920 --> 00:30:41.320
Both: ...from this day
until the end of my days.

362
00:30:45.240 --> 00:30:47.920
- Is that safe?
- They're long gone.

363
00:30:53.040 --> 00:30:57.160
You were right. I can get inside
Summer's mind whenever I want.

364
00:30:57.320 --> 00:30:59.960
Of course you can.

365
00:31:00.120 --> 00:31:03.640
North of the Wall there are wildlings
who can control all sorts of animals.

366
00:31:05.240 --> 00:31:08.600
But you did a lot more than that.

367
00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:11.480
You got inside Hodor's mind.

368
00:31:12.720 --> 00:31:15.840
They can't do that north of the Wall?

369
00:31:16.840 --> 00:31:19.360
No one can do that... anywhere.

370
00:31:26.320 --> 00:31:29.280
When I was looking
through Summer's eyes. I saw Jon.

371
00:31:29.440 --> 00:31:31.320
- Where?
- He was with the wildlings.

372
00:31:31.480 --> 00:31:33.680
They tried to kill him.
but he got away.

373
00:31:33.840 --> 00:31:35.400
Osha: He'll be heading back
to Castle Black. then.

374
00:31:35.560 --> 00:31:37.200
That's where we should go.

375
00:31:37.360 --> 00:31:39.600
For all we know.
Castle Black's already under attack.

376
00:31:39.760 --> 00:31:41.080
If this many wildlings got through

377
00:31:41.240 --> 00:31:45.080
I already told you.
I'm not going north of the Wall.

378
00:31:45.240 --> 00:31:49.040
Everything Jojen told me is true.

379
00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:51.040
You saw what I did to Hodor.

380
00:31:51.200 --> 00:31:52.960
I have to find the three-eyed raven.

381
00:31:53.120 --> 00:31:54.520
Listen to me. little lord.

382
00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:58.600
Don't worry.
I'm not asking you to come with me.

383
00:32:00.800 --> 00:32:02.280
It won't be safe for Rickon.

384
00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:05.280
Me? I'm coming with you.

385
00:32:05.440 --> 00:32:07.720
No.

386
00:32:07.880 --> 00:32:10.120
You and Osha and Shaggydog
head for the Last Hearth.

387
00:32:10.280 --> 00:32:13.360
The Umbers are our bannermen.
They'll protect you.

388
00:32:13.520 --> 00:32:15.320
I'm coming with you.

389
00:32:15.480 --> 00:32:17.040
I'm your brother.

390
00:32:17.200 --> 00:32:21.200
I have to protect you.

391
00:32:21.360 --> 00:32:24.560
Right now I have to protect you.

392
00:32:24.720 --> 00:32:27.440
Robb's at war
and I'm going beyond the Wall.

393
00:32:27.600 --> 00:32:32.360
If something happens to us.
you're the heir to Winterfell.

394
00:32:33.760 --> 00:32:35.520
Would you know
how to find the Last Hearth?

395
00:32:35.680 --> 00:32:38.840
You southerners build
your big castles and you never move.

396
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:40.840
You're easy to find.

397
00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:45.880
We're not southerners.
And I don't want to leave you.

398
00:32:46.040 --> 00:32:50.000
Shh. shh.
Come here. little soldier.

399
00:32:50.160 --> 00:32:53.440
You and me.
we're gonna have some adventures.

400
00:32:53.600 --> 00:32:55.640
You don't have to do any of this.

401
00:32:55.800 --> 00:32:57.120
( crying )

402
00:32:57.280 --> 00:32:58.600
Your family took me in

403
00:32:58.760 --> 00:33:02.160
and was good to me
when they had no cause to be.

404
00:33:02.320 --> 00:33:05.280
Shh. We'll be fine. you and me.

405
00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:07.440
The Umbers are great warriors.

406
00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:10.160
Even I heard about them growing up.

407
00:33:10.320 --> 00:33:12.920
They'll teach you
how to swing a sword.

408
00:33:13.080 --> 00:33:15.440
I know how to swing a sword.

409
00:33:18.680 --> 00:33:21.040
( kisses )

410
00:33:22.760 --> 00:33:24.920
You're leaving now?
It's the middle of the night.

411
00:33:25.080 --> 00:33:27.960
I learned to walk in darkness.

412
00:33:29.240 --> 00:33:30.560
Say your good-byes. little man.

413
00:33:38.440 --> 00:33:40.320
Keep this one safe.

414
00:33:42.360 --> 00:33:44.000
He means the world to me.

415
00:34:04.880 --> 00:34:07.200
We've been waiting a long time.

416
00:34:09.160 --> 00:34:12.160
Haven't we?

417
00:34:12.320 --> 00:34:15.480
I don't know. you tell me.
How long does it take to sack a city?

418
00:34:23.960 --> 00:34:26.080
It was just as you said.

419
00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:28.760
They did not believe
until it was too late.

420
00:34:28.920 --> 00:34:34.000
Their slave soldiers threw down
their spears and surrendered.

421
00:34:38.440 --> 00:34:40.400
And Daario Naharis?

422
00:34:45.720 --> 00:34:47.720
( footsteps )

423
00:35:00.560 --> 00:35:02.640
The city is yours. my queen.

424
00:35:02.800 --> 00:35:06.200
( music playing )

425
00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:09.720
( people laughing. chatting )

426
00:35:25.200 --> 00:35:26.520
They're good. aren't they?

427
00:35:26.680 --> 00:35:28.280
They ought to be
because they cost enough.

428
00:35:28.440 --> 00:35:29.880
( laughs )

429
00:35:30.040 --> 00:35:32.400
( laughs )

430
00:35:35.440 --> 00:35:38.920
- Look at the crowd there.
- ( Catelyn laughs )

431
00:35:41.560 --> 00:35:43.400
He complained about this marriage

432
00:35:43.560 --> 00:35:46.880
the entire ride from Riverrun.
and now look at him.

433
00:35:47.040 --> 00:35:49.080
Blackfish:
The gods love to reward a fool.

434
00:35:49.240 --> 00:35:51.400
- Uncle.
- What?

435
00:35:51.560 --> 00:35:56.320
He's my nephew. I love him.
And he's a damned fool.

436
00:35:56.480 --> 00:35:58.480
( chuckles )

437
00:36:01.640 --> 00:36:03.640
Don't you drink. Lord Bolton?

438
00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:05.880
Never do. my lady.
Dulls the senses.

439
00:36:06.040 --> 00:36:08.080
That's the point.

440
00:36:08.240 --> 00:36:09.960
Didn't you marry
one of these Frey girls?

441
00:36:10.120 --> 00:36:11.480
Aye.

442
00:36:11.640 --> 00:36:13.520
Lord Walder let me
choose any of his granddaughters

443
00:36:13.680 --> 00:36:17.400
and promised me the girl's weight
in silver as a dowry.

444
00:36:17.560 --> 00:36:19.160
So I have a fat young bride.

445
00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:21.000
( laughs )

446
00:36:21.160 --> 00:36:22.960
I hope she makes you very happy.

447
00:36:23.120 --> 00:36:24.720
Well. she's made me very rich.

448
00:36:24.880 --> 00:36:27.280
Pardon. my lord. my lady.

449
00:36:27.440 --> 00:36:29.560
I need to find a tree to piss on.

450
00:36:31.960 --> 00:36:35.320
My mother's alone with Roose Bolton.
I should rescue her.

451
00:36:35.480 --> 00:36:39.120
Your mother is less in need of rescue
than any woman I've ever met.

452
00:36:39.280 --> 00:36:43.760
Be kind.
She's finally starting to like you.

453
00:36:43.920 --> 00:36:45.320
And I like her.

454
00:36:45.480 --> 00:36:48.600
But if she had her way.
I would be back in Volantis

455
00:36:48.760 --> 00:36:51.800
playing my harp
and you would be sitting over there

456
00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:54.760
eating blackberries
out of Roslin Frey's hand.

457
00:36:54.920 --> 00:36:56.720
Perhaps I've made
a terrible mistake.

458
00:36:56.880 --> 00:36:59.480
( scoffs )

459
00:36:59.640 --> 00:37:02.200
Striking your king
is an act of treason.

460
00:37:05.640 --> 00:37:08.640
No. don't.

461
00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:11.160
Don't insult them.

462
00:37:12.400 --> 00:37:14.080
Your Grace.

463
00:37:14.240 --> 00:37:17.000
( pounding on tables )

464
00:37:19.160 --> 00:37:20.760
( pounding stops )

465
00:37:20.920 --> 00:37:26.600
The septon has prayed his prayers.
some words were said.

466
00:37:26.760 --> 00:37:31.240
and Lord Edmure has wrapped
my daughter in a cloak.

467
00:37:31.400 --> 00:37:35.520
But they are not yet
man and wife.

468
00:37:35.680 --> 00:37:37.320
A sword needs a sheath.

469
00:37:37.480 --> 00:37:39.320
( guests laughing )

470
00:37:39.480 --> 00:37:44.000
( laughs )

471
00:37:44.160 --> 00:37:46.040
And a wedding needs a bedding.

472
00:37:46.200 --> 00:37:47.520
( guests cheering )

473
00:37:47.680 --> 00:37:49.000
What does my sire say?

474
00:37:49.160 --> 00:37:50.560
( guests chanting )

475
00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:57.400
To bed! To bed! To bed!

476
00:37:57.560 --> 00:37:59.480
If you think the time is right.
Lord Walder.

477
00:37:59.640 --> 00:38:03.520
by all means. let us bed them.

478
00:38:03.680 --> 00:38:06.120
( guests cheering )

479
00:38:06.280 --> 00:38:10.240
( music playing )

480
00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:13.800
( chanting )
To bed! To bed! To bed!

481
00:38:18.680 --> 00:38:20.480
Man:
Go on!

482
00:38:37.680 --> 00:38:40.640
Oh! Careful now. ladies.

483
00:38:40.800 --> 00:38:45.240
Once you set that monster free.
there's no caging him again.

484
00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:49.280
( chanting continues )
To bed! To bed! To bed!

485
00:38:52.120 --> 00:38:53.640
Poor girl.

486
00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:56.400
Every bride suffers the same.

487
00:38:56.560 --> 00:38:58.920
I'm sure
you endured yours with grace.

488
00:38:59.080 --> 00:39:02.680
Oh. Ned forbade it.
He said it wouldn't be right

489
00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:04.400
if he broke a man's jaw
on our wedding night.

490
00:39:04.560 --> 00:39:07.120
( chuckles )

491
00:39:12.800 --> 00:39:15.920
That is a very strange custom.

492
00:39:16.080 --> 00:39:19.200
I suppose it does seem strange
from a foreigner's perspective.

493
00:39:19.360 --> 00:39:22.960
- It seems normal to you?
- It's a tradition.

494
00:39:25.080 --> 00:39:27.560
Without the bedding ceremony.
there's no real proof

495
00:39:27.720 --> 00:39:29.960
the lord and lady consummated
their marriage.

496
00:39:30.120 --> 00:39:34.320
But there are other ways
of providing proof.

497
00:39:35.840 --> 00:39:37.160
Boy or girl?

498
00:39:40.040 --> 00:39:41.360
I don't know.

499
00:39:41.520 --> 00:39:44.240
But if it's a boy.
I know what we should name him.

500
00:39:44.400 --> 00:39:46.520
Oh. do you?

501
00:39:46.680 --> 00:39:49.720
It seems to me the father should have
some say in his son's naming.

502
00:39:49.880 --> 00:39:53.480
Eddard.

503
00:39:54.920 --> 00:39:58.920
Don't you want to teach
little Ned Stark how to ride horses?

504
00:39:59.080 --> 00:40:00.880
I do.

505
00:40:28.400 --> 00:40:31.080
( band playing
"Rains of Castamere" )

506
00:40:46.680 --> 00:40:49.360
( wolf whining )

507
00:40:51.800 --> 00:40:54.720
( whines )

508
00:40:54.880 --> 00:40:56.840
Man:
Go on. line 'em up!

509
00:40:57.000 --> 00:41:01.200
( chatter. laughter )

510
00:41:03.680 --> 00:41:05.760
( laughing )

511
00:41:13.240 --> 00:41:14.880
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.

512
00:41:18.280 --> 00:41:21.240
- Where are you going?
- Got salt pork for the feast.

513
00:41:21.400 --> 00:41:23.600
The feast is over.

514
00:41:23.760 --> 00:41:25.840
Hound:
Doesn't sound like it's over.

515
00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:28.680
If I tell you it's over. it's over.

516
00:41:28.840 --> 00:41:32.960
Turn this cart around
and get the hell out of here.

517
00:41:33.120 --> 00:41:34.480
Got pig's feet. too.

518
00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:39.280
Are you soft in the head?
Turn this cart around.

519
00:41:49.920 --> 00:41:51.440
( music stops )

520
00:41:51.600 --> 00:41:52.960
Your Grace.

521
00:41:59.000 --> 00:42:04.720
I feel I've been remiss in my duties.

522
00:42:04.880 --> 00:42:08.200
I've given you meat
and wine and music.

523
00:42:08.360 --> 00:42:13.560
but I haven't shown you
the hospitality you deserve.

524
00:42:15.320 --> 00:42:20.040
My king has married and I owe
my new queen a wedding gift.

525
00:42:24.240 --> 00:42:26.400
Robb!

526
00:42:29.240 --> 00:42:31.000
( gasping )

527
00:42:46.520 --> 00:42:48.760
( grunts )

528
00:42:50.640 --> 00:42:52.160
( screams continue )

529
00:42:55.000 --> 00:42:57.200
( screaming )

530
00:43:09.880 --> 00:43:11.200
( men laughing )

531
00:43:11.360 --> 00:43:13.320
Stark soldier: You ready
to head home to Winterfell. right?

532
00:43:13.480 --> 00:43:16.440
( men laughing )

533
00:43:16.600 --> 00:43:18.000
Stark soldier:
Feast over yet. is it?

534
00:43:18.160 --> 00:43:20.320
Aye. it's over.

535
00:43:20.480 --> 00:43:23.280
( men screaming )

536
00:43:32.360 --> 00:43:35.080
( wolf howling )

537
00:43:35.240 --> 00:43:36.720
- ( banging )
- ( growling )

538
00:43:46.920 --> 00:43:49.560
( growling )

539
00:43:49.720 --> 00:43:51.120
Guard:
Follow him.

540
00:43:53.440 --> 00:43:55.880
- Aim!
- ( snarling )

541
00:43:56.040 --> 00:43:57.440
( growls )

542
00:43:57.600 --> 00:44:00.640
( wolf whines )

543
00:44:03.920 --> 00:44:07.120
( guard shouting )

544
00:44:11.800 --> 00:44:15.040
( groaning )

545
00:44:16.640 --> 00:44:18.280
( guards shouting )

546
00:44:23.400 --> 00:44:25.480
It's too late.

547
00:44:39.320 --> 00:44:41.560
- ( grunting )
- ( fighting continues )

548
00:45:03.360 --> 00:45:04.840
( chuckles )

549
00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:08.240
The King in the North arises.

550
00:45:08.400 --> 00:45:10.000
( chuckles )

551
00:45:28.600 --> 00:45:30.600
Lord Walder!

552
00:45:30.760 --> 00:45:32.160
Lord Walder. enough!

553
00:45:32.320 --> 00:45:34.440
Let it end!

554
00:45:36.200 --> 00:45:38.080
Please.

555
00:45:38.240 --> 00:45:40.120
He is my son.

556
00:45:40.280 --> 00:45:42.480
My first son.

557
00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:44.880
Let him go and I swear
that we will forget this.

558
00:45:45.040 --> 00:45:47.560
I swear it
by the old gods and new.

559
00:45:47.720 --> 00:45:49.040
We will take no vengeance.

560
00:45:49.200 --> 00:45:52.560
You already swore me one oath
right here in my castle.

561
00:45:52.720 --> 00:45:56.160
You swore by all the gods
your son would marry my daughter!

562
00:45:56.320 --> 00:45:59.360
Catelyn: Take me for a hostage.
but let Robb go.

563
00:45:59.520 --> 00:46:01.640
Robb. get up.

564
00:46:01.800 --> 00:46:05.400
Get up and walk out. Please!

565
00:46:07.120 --> 00:46:09.720
Please!

566
00:46:09.880 --> 00:46:13.920
And why would I let him do that?

567
00:46:16.320 --> 00:46:22.120
On my honor as a Tully.
on my honor as a Stark.

568
00:46:22.280 --> 00:46:28.160
let him go
or I will cut your wife's throat.

569
00:46:35.360 --> 00:46:37.600
I'll find another.

570
00:46:40.680 --> 00:46:42.640
Mother.

571
00:46:43.960 --> 00:46:45.400
The Lannisters send their regards.

572
00:46:45.560 --> 00:46:48.240
( knife pierces )

573
00:46:55.960 --> 00:46:57.920
( wails )

574
00:47:01.840 --> 00:47:03.920
( knife clatters )
